## Findings

[R5-F1] **MEDIUM** — non-string fold keys lose type identity across addresses and provenance.

`_row_key` correctly retains accepted keys but stringifies them ([surface.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/apps/loops/src/loops/surface.py:527)). Source-fact buckets likewise use string addresses ([vertex_reader.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py:455)), while provenance replay folds the native payload and then looks it up using the CLI string key ([provenance.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/apps/loops/src/loops/provenance.py:165)).

Observed consequences:

- Numeric `0`: `decision/0 --why --json` exited 0 with `total_facts: 1`, but `fields: []` and an empty `changed` list.
- Boolean `False` reproduces the same empty attribution; string `"0"` works normally.
- Numeric `0` and string `"0"` in the same kind remain two engine-folded items but project to duplicate `decision/0` rows, while their source facts combine into one `decision/0` bucket.

This is silent provenance/identity loss for keys the ruling explicitly declares valid.

